# Line endings, settled here rather than per machine.
#
# tools/build_docs.py writes generated files through Python's text mode,
# which emits CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux. Without this, a rebuild on
# a Windows bench machine and a rebuild in CI produce byte-different
# files from identical inputs - and the byte-equality guard in
# tests/test_docs.py is what makes the generated pages trustworthy.
#
# The tests would not have caught it, because Python reads with universal
# newlines and compares both forms equal. It surfaced as thirty files
# showing as modified with no content change, which was enough to block
# a `git switch`.
* text=auto

# Markdown is LF in the working tree as well as in the repository, so
# what the generator writes on Windows matches what it writes in CI.
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# Golden files are compared byte-for-byte.
*.json text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
